WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.868
-Hello, everyone, and welcome
back to the attic.

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:05.105
Last week you may recall
we addressed speculation

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:08.641
about the sudden disappearance
of my copy of "The Thorn Birds,"

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.477
the 1977 Australian romance
novel that inspired

00:00:11.477 --> 00:00:13.279
the hit 1983 miniseries

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:15.347
starring a frequently shirtless
Richard Chamberlain.

00:00:15.347 --> 00:00:18.451
In 1983, it turns out that was
the exact right amount

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:20.186
of chest hair for a leading man.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:22.388
Chamberlain never would have
survived in these hairless times

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:24.824
we're living in, where our
sex symbols are all Chrises

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:27.326
with chests smooth enough
to eat off.

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:29.762
Anyway, the point is, I left
the window open overnight

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:31.965
to get rid of the wasps,
but then "The Thorn Birds"

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:34.500
flew out, we think,
because it's mating season.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.369
But as you can see,
Thorny is back

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:38.704
and maybe with child?
Impossible to tell.

00:00:38.704 --> 00:00:40.807
Meanwhile, the president is
pregnant with rage --

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:44.010
that's a segue, a bad one,
but technically still a segue --

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.612
and decided to give up
in the fight against coronavirus

00:00:46.612 --> 00:00:48.314
in order to reopen the economy.

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:50.716
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:50.716 --> 00:00:54.387
♪♪

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:57.156
You would think that
putting aside his venality,

00:00:57.156 --> 00:00:59.592
his narcissism,
and his deadly incompetence,

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:02.162
Donald Trump could
at the very least muster

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:04.397
a little empathy for the victims
of this pandemic,

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:05.765
their loved ones,
and the millions

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.700
who have
put themselves in harm's way,

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.302
lost jobs, or made tremendous
personal sacrifices

00:01:10.302 --> 00:01:11.470
during this crisis.

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:12.772
But of course,
he can't do that,

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.841
because he's incapable
of empathy.

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:17.243
He only has two emotions --
boredom and rage.

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:19.078
He's either staring off
into the distance

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:21.181
while someone talks
about complex policy details

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:23.149
or hissing at reporters
like a snake

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.750
whose nest was just disturbed.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.353
In fact, just listen to
the cold, detached way in which

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:29.689
Trump talked about allowing
Americans to die

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:31.657
in order to reopen the economy

00:01:31.657 --> 00:01:33.726
and the 30 million people
who have lost jobs

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:35.295
because of his handling
of this crisis

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:37.063
during an interview on ABC
yesterday.

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:38.998
-Do you believe that's
the reality we're facing?

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:41.901
That lives will be lost to
reopen the country?

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:44.603
-It's possible there will be
some, because you won't be

00:01:44.603 --> 00:01:48.707
locked into an apartment
or a house or whatever it is.

00:01:48.707 --> 00:01:51.744
-There are 30 million
Americans who are unemployed.

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:53.312
You don't need me
to tell you that.

00:01:53.312 --> 00:01:55.648
We're expecting the new
unemployment rate this week.

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:58.852
There have been forecasts,
15, 16, 17%.

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:02.822
One of your advisers projected
an unemployment rate of 19%.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:06.592
That's nearly one in five
Americans without a job.

00:02:06.592 --> 00:02:09.395
How bad is this going to get?

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:11.363
-Well, that is what it is.

00:02:11.363 --> 00:02:13.499
-Wow. What soaring words.

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:15.734
It reminds me of
Martin Luther King's

00:02:15.734 --> 00:02:17.870
"I slept pretty good
last night" speech.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:20.240
Or FDR's famous response
when they told him

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:24.143
about Pearl Harbor --
"Well, [bleep] happens."

00:02:24.143 --> 00:02:26.512
Usually when someone is that
soulless and dead-eyed,

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:28.547
you're not asking them questions
about the economy,

00:02:28.547 --> 00:02:30.083
you're holding up
a Rorschach test.

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:31.717
"And what is this, Donald?"

00:02:31.717 --> 00:02:33.719
[ As Trump ]
"It is what it is.

00:02:33.719 --> 00:02:36.555
"Very, very interesting.
Okay, guards,

00:02:36.555 --> 00:02:38.391
you can put him back
in his restraints now."

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:41.294
"Oh, I don't think the guards
can hear you."

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:43.596
"Donald, what have you done?"

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:45.965
Yesterday Trump also made his
first major trip in months

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:49.134
to tour a Honeywell factory in
Arizona, a trip that gave us

00:02:49.134 --> 00:02:52.471
what may end up as one of the
enduring images of this crisis.

00:02:52.471 --> 00:02:55.374
Trump toured a mask factory
as his White House signaled

00:02:55.374 --> 00:02:56.942
they were basically
just giving up

00:02:56.942 --> 00:02:58.945
on suppressing
the coronavirus pandemic

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:01.113
to focus on reopening
the economy instead.

00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:02.948
And has he was doing that,

00:03:02.948 --> 00:03:05.485
someone chose to blast
"Live and Let Die"

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:06.652
on the speakers.

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:09.689
-The material traps
the particulates.

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:12.224
-♪ Live and let die ♪

00:03:12.224 --> 00:03:16.295
♪♪

00:03:16.295 --> 00:03:19.265
-Wow.
Welcome to the resistance,

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:22.401
Honeywell factory floor
deejay?

00:03:22.401 --> 00:03:24.070
Doesn't get much more
on the nose than that.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.138
What were the other songs on
that play list?

00:03:26.138 --> 00:03:29.976
-♪ It's the end of the world
as we know it ♪

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:34.179
♪ It's the end of the world
as we know it ♪

00:03:34.179 --> 00:03:36.482
-You can hear all those
classic hits and more

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.751
on "Now That's What I Call
Symbolism."

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:41.387
"Live and Let Die" playing while
Trump tours a mask factory

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.289
during a pandemic
is the surest sign yet

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:44.857
that we're living
in a video game.

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.759
And if we are in a video game,
does anyone have the cheat code

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:48.327
to get rid of wasps?

00:03:48.327 --> 00:03:49.929
Because I tried up, up, down,
down, left, right, left, right,

00:03:49.929 --> 00:03:52.198
B, A, start, and that just
made them angrier.

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:54.266
Anyway, sure enough,
during that same trip,

00:03:54.266 --> 00:03:56.535
Trump brushed off the
growing death toll

00:03:56.535 --> 00:03:58.303
and said he was eager
to force Americans

00:03:58.303 --> 00:03:59.805
back to work prematurely,

00:03:59.805 --> 00:04:02.741
telling them to think of
themselves as participants

00:04:02.741 --> 00:04:04.610
in an armed conflict.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:07.446
-And you see what's going on.
They have to open.

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:12.051
And the people of our country
should think of themselves

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:13.986
as warriors.

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:15.788
Our country has to open.

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:19.792
I'm viewing our great citizens
of this country

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:23.562
to a certain extent and to
a large extent as warriors.

00:04:23.562 --> 00:04:25.397
They're warriors.

00:04:25.397 --> 00:04:26.799
We can't keep our country
closed.

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:28.268
We have to open our country.

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:30.235
The people of our country
are warriors.

00:04:30.235 --> 00:04:31.504
And I'm looking at it.

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:33.840
I'm not saying anything
is perfect.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.208
And yes, will some people
be affected? Yes.

00:04:36.208 --> 00:04:38.544
Will some people be affected
badly? Yes.

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:40.680
But we have to get
our country open,

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.448
and we have to get it open
soon.

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:44.884
And I said it before
and I'll say it again.

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:47.286
The people of our country
are warriors.

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:49.989
-That's right, Trump wants
you -- you to be a warrior

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:52.891
while he sits safely in
isolation in the White House.

00:04:52.891 --> 00:04:56.129
"I would join in, but I feel
another bone spur coming on,

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:58.597
which is devastating to me,
because the last one happened

00:04:58.597 --> 00:05:00.800
right before the Vietnam War.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.736
I mean, what are the chances
that it happens again now?

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:05.104
I mean --"

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:06.872
This is truly sadistic.

00:05:06.872 --> 00:05:09.675
The president is telling you
to go out and face off

00:05:09.675 --> 00:05:12.077
against a deadly virus all for
the sake of the stock market.

00:05:12.077 --> 00:05:14.546
The only way that could be more
out of touch is if he said it

00:05:14.546 --> 00:05:16.048
while dousing himself in Purell

00:05:16.048 --> 00:05:18.383
and holding a 36-pack
of toilet paper.

00:05:18.383 --> 00:05:20.886
Every day it seems we pass
a grim new milestone

00:05:20.886 --> 00:05:24.556
in the coronavirus pandemic,
with more than 70,000 Americans

00:05:24.556 --> 00:05:26.959
now dead and at least
30 million out of work,

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:29.261
which, according to Trump
means it's a perfect time

00:05:29.261 --> 00:05:31.264
to stand down
and wrap things up.

00:05:31.264 --> 00:05:33.932
-We can't keep our country
closed for the next five years.

00:05:33.932 --> 00:05:35.634
You know, you could say there
might be a recurrence,

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:37.036
and there might be.

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:39.705
And, you know, most doctors,
or some doctors say

00:05:39.705 --> 00:05:41.707
that it will happen.

00:05:41.707 --> 00:05:44.410
And it will be a flame and we're
going to put the flame out.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:45.811
We've learned a lot, you know.

00:05:45.811 --> 00:05:48.247
We've learned a lot about
the coronavirus.

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:50.716
-First of all, who's "we"?
You haven't learned anything.

00:05:50.716 --> 00:05:52.418
Whenever the doctors
are up there talking,

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:53.819
you do that thing
where you zone out

00:05:53.819 --> 00:05:55.655
and sway back
and forth like a drunk guy

00:05:55.655 --> 00:05:57.423
who's trying to pretend
he's sober.

00:05:57.423 --> 00:06:00.093
And then you get back up to the
podium having only heard, like,

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:02.561
three words and try to sound
like you know what's going on.

00:06:02.561 --> 00:06:05.798
"So what I'm hearing is -- what
I grasped when the scientists

00:06:05.798 --> 00:06:08.967
were talking, is that powerful
lights will cure the coronavirus

00:06:08.967 --> 00:06:10.470
and give you superpowers.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:12.471
You know, I saw that
in a documentary once.

00:06:12.471 --> 00:06:14.373
Only down -- turns you green.

00:06:14.373 --> 00:06:16.576
That's the downside side effect.

00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:20.412
So still --
still pretty promising news."

00:06:20.412 --> 00:06:22.414
You are incapable of learning.

00:06:22.414 --> 00:06:24.584
You showed up to the CDC
in Atlanta surrounded by

00:06:24.584 --> 00:06:26.685
some of the best doctors
in the world and all you did

00:06:26.685 --> 00:06:28.955
was hold up a printout
of a virus like a kid

00:06:28.955 --> 00:06:31.423
who forgot to do his science
project until the last minute.

00:06:31.423 --> 00:06:35.961
"As you can see here, the virus
is called Wikipedia.

00:06:35.961 --> 00:06:40.966
Side effects include further
reading and external links."

00:06:40.966 --> 00:06:43.035
Although actually I will
give Trump credit.

00:06:43.035 --> 00:06:45.937
In the span of two months, he
did at least learn one thing --

00:06:45.937 --> 00:06:47.706
the name of the virus.

00:06:47.706 --> 00:06:51.010
-So you can't put them down
in the, uh, in the category

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:55.915
of the overall population in
terms of this, uh, corona flu.

00:06:55.915 --> 00:06:58.117
-Yes, corona flu.

00:06:58.117 --> 00:07:00.553
Remember when a deadly virus
was racing across the globe

00:07:00.553 --> 00:07:02.888
and the president was getting
intelligence reports about it,

00:07:02.888 --> 00:07:04.490
and he got the name wrong,

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:06.892
like the worst member
of your bar trivia team?

00:07:06.892 --> 00:07:10.796
"This English rock band is led
by front man Mick Jagger."

00:07:10.796 --> 00:07:13.366
"Oh, I know,
it's The Rolling Scones.

00:07:13.366 --> 00:07:16.969
Rolling -- In America they're
called The Rolling Muffins.

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:19.605
That's an extra piece
of trivia."

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:21.574
Second, no one,
and I mean no one,

00:07:21.574 --> 00:07:23.476
wants to keep the country
closed for five years.

00:07:23.476 --> 00:07:25.143
It hasn't even been closed
for five months

00:07:25.143 --> 00:07:26.512
and we're already losing
our minds.

00:07:26.512 --> 00:07:28.514
I spend six hours a day
washing my hands,

00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:30.982
I wipe down every package like
it's coated in anthrax.

00:07:30.982 --> 00:07:33.952
I've watched so much Netflix
that my home page says,

00:07:33.952 --> 00:07:37.156
"We have nothing left for you.
Try Hulu?"

00:07:37.156 --> 00:07:40.892
And I've inhaled so much Lysol,
my urine smells like lemon zest.

00:07:40.892 --> 00:07:42.862
No one wants to live like this.

00:07:42.862 --> 00:07:44.196
In fact, we didn't have to.

00:07:44.196 --> 00:07:45.964
Lots of other major
developed countries

00:07:45.964 --> 00:07:48.434
have successfully suppressed
their outbreaks by acting early,

00:07:48.434 --> 00:07:50.469
testing aggressively,
and implementing a system

00:07:50.469 --> 00:07:53.439
of isolating cases and tracing
their contacts.

00:07:53.439 --> 00:07:55.942
Some never even had to fully
lock down, and others

00:07:55.942 --> 00:07:57.877
have already reopened,
like in South Korea,

00:07:57.877 --> 00:07:59.979
where they had their
first case on the exact same day

00:07:59.979 --> 00:08:01.247
we had ours.

00:08:01.247 --> 00:08:02.681
And while here in the U.S.,

00:08:02.681 --> 00:08:05.684
almost every day at least 25,000
new coronavirus cases

00:08:05.684 --> 00:08:07.619
are identified,
in South Korea,

00:08:07.619 --> 00:08:10.522
the rate of new confirmed cases
of coronavirus has slowed down

00:08:10.522 --> 00:08:13.726
dramatically in recent weeks
to less than ten a day.

00:08:13.726 --> 00:08:15.260
Of course if you pointed
that out to Trump,

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:16.561
he probably wouldn't accept it.

00:08:16.561 --> 00:08:18.030
"It's not a fair compar--

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:21.300
South Korea is 13 hours ahead,
so they had a jump on it."

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:23.602
In fact, while we're all stuck
in our homes watching reruns

00:08:23.602 --> 00:08:25.303
of "Blue Bloods" at 2:00
in the afternoon,

00:08:25.303 --> 00:08:27.139
Korean baseball is already
back playing games,

00:08:27.139 --> 00:08:28.507
just without fans.

00:08:28.507 --> 00:08:31.343
In fact, ESPN is now airing them
here in the U.S.,

00:08:31.343 --> 00:08:33.412
which has introduced us
to some truly incredible

00:08:33.412 --> 00:08:36.982
team names, like the
NC Dinos and the SK Wyverns,

00:08:36.982 --> 00:08:39.518
which are mythical winged
two-legged dragons

00:08:39.518 --> 00:08:41.186
with barbed tails.

00:08:41.186 --> 00:08:43.622
Last year they even used
augmented reality

00:08:43.622 --> 00:08:46.959
to have a dragon fly into
the stadium and breathe fire.

00:08:46.959 --> 00:08:49.829
Our baseball teams need
more mascots like that.

00:08:49.829 --> 00:08:52.164
The only mythical creature
we have is, I don't know,

00:08:52.164 --> 00:08:54.733
is it like an aardvark?

00:08:54.733 --> 00:08:58.470
Like a -- like a hairy aardvark
who loves baseball?

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:00.072
Hmm.

00:09:00.072 --> 00:09:01.841
We've been highlighting
success stories like that

00:09:01.841 --> 00:09:04.543
from South Korea to Iceland
to New Zealand to Taiwan

00:09:04.543 --> 00:09:05.978
because they're out there.

00:09:05.978 --> 00:09:08.314
There are lots of countries
with competent governments

00:09:08.314 --> 00:09:09.815
that managed to suppress
the outbreak

00:09:09.815 --> 00:09:11.884
and allow their societies to
safely return

00:09:11.884 --> 00:09:13.719
to some semblance of normalcy.

00:09:13.719 --> 00:09:16.455
Trump has repeatedly lied
and claimed that, as he put it,

00:09:16.455 --> 00:09:19.024
the cupboards were bare when
he took office three years ago

00:09:19.024 --> 00:09:20.693
and that's why he's failed
to fight the virus.

00:09:20.693 --> 00:09:22.628
But in a new ABC interview,
Trump was asked

00:09:22.628 --> 00:09:25.064
why he didn't do anything
to fix the situation.

00:09:25.064 --> 00:09:26.766
-You're three years
into your first term.

00:09:26.766 --> 00:09:27.933
-Yeah.
-You're now applying

00:09:27.933 --> 00:09:29.168
for the job again.

00:09:29.168 --> 00:09:31.003
What did you do when you
became president

00:09:31.003 --> 00:09:33.472
to restock those cupboards
that you say were bare?

00:09:33.472 --> 00:09:35.174
-Well, I'll be honest, uh,

00:09:35.174 --> 00:09:36.975
I have a lot of things
going on.

00:09:36.975 --> 00:09:39.411
-No, you don't.
All you do is watch TV,

00:09:39.411 --> 00:09:41.781
and whenever your aides let you
out of your straitjacket, tweet.

00:09:41.781 --> 00:09:44.083
And when you're not golfing,
you're tweeting about golfing.

00:09:44.083 --> 00:09:47.186
Like on Sunday, when you
retweeted a post

00:09:47.186 --> 00:09:48.721
from your golf course
in Scotland claiming

00:09:48.721 --> 00:09:51.457
they had been named best golf
course in the UK and Ireland

00:09:51.457 --> 00:09:53.358
by a European golf magazine.

00:09:53.358 --> 00:09:56.195
"So nice to see this
great honor, thank you,

00:09:56.195 --> 00:09:58.063
but haven't played golf
in a long time."

00:09:58.063 --> 00:10:00.099
First of all, that's not true.
You played golf in March

00:10:00.099 --> 00:10:02.201
with members of
the Washington Nationals.

00:10:02.201 --> 00:10:03.903
Damn it, Nationals!

00:10:03.903 --> 00:10:05.571
You were supposed to be
the feel-good team

00:10:05.571 --> 00:10:07.773
everyone could be happy with
over the cheating Astros.

00:10:07.773 --> 00:10:09.942
Now, I mean, who are
we supposed root for

00:10:09.942 --> 00:10:12.110
when baseball comes back,
the Mets?

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:13.679
I mean, they're the only team
that's doing better

00:10:13.679 --> 00:10:15.347
during quarantine.

00:10:15.347 --> 00:10:16.915
Pretty sure the last president
they met with

00:10:16.915 --> 00:10:20.085
was William Henry Harrison,
and then he died ten days later.

00:10:20.085 --> 00:10:22.888
That was the year Mr. Met
caught typhoid.

00:10:22.888 --> 00:10:25.124
And now, instead of taking
any responsibility

00:10:25.124 --> 00:10:27.827
for the situation, Trump
and his toadies on state TV

00:10:27.827 --> 00:10:29.662
are whining that he
hasn't gotten enough credit

00:10:29.662 --> 00:10:32.064
for only letting
70,000 Americans die

00:10:32.064 --> 00:10:33.565
and 30 million
lose their jobs,

00:10:33.565 --> 00:10:35.600
like human beer keg
Jesse Watters

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:37.402
on Fox News this week.

00:10:37.402 --> 00:10:39.771
-Can you imagine, Greg,
the media, how they'd sound

00:10:39.771 --> 00:10:42.508
if Barack Obama were president
during the pandemic?

00:10:42.508 --> 00:10:44.476
It'd go something like this --

00:10:44.476 --> 00:10:48.447
"Barack Obama, putting politics
aside and sacrificing,

00:10:48.447 --> 00:10:51.016
the key to a successful
reelection,

00:10:51.016 --> 00:10:54.754
shut down the economy just
in order to save lives."

00:10:54.754 --> 00:10:56.488
That's what it would sound like.

00:10:56.488 --> 00:10:58.690
Now, I know the president's
not going to get

00:10:58.690 --> 00:10:59.959
great coverage like that,

00:10:59.959 --> 00:11:02.628
but the president just wants
fair coverage,

00:11:02.628 --> 00:11:04.896
because he never got credit
for winning the election.

00:11:04.896 --> 00:11:06.599
They said Russia cheated.

00:11:06.599 --> 00:11:08.501
He never got credit
for the economy.

00:11:08.501 --> 00:11:10.436
They said it was Barack Obama's.

00:11:10.436 --> 00:11:12.471
And he's not getting credit
for anything,

00:11:12.471 --> 00:11:14.807
for ventilators,
for flattening the curve.

00:11:14.807 --> 00:11:17.376
-My God, you sound like
the whiniest pledge

00:11:17.376 --> 00:11:18.777
in Sigma Chi.

00:11:18.777 --> 00:11:21.146
"The dean is shutting down
our blackface party,

00:11:21.146 --> 00:11:23.281
completely ignoring the fact
it was a fundraiser

00:11:23.281 --> 00:11:25.918
to help local cocaine dealers."

00:11:25.918 --> 00:11:28.287
The U.S. is the richest and most
powerful country on Earth,

00:11:28.287 --> 00:11:30.923
and yet we're also the epicenter
of a deadly outbreak

00:11:30.923 --> 00:11:32.858
that has been suppressed
in lots of other countries.

00:11:32.858 --> 00:11:35.294
And now the president
wants to send you to war

00:11:35.294 --> 00:11:37.562
against the virus for the sake
of the stock market.

00:11:37.562 --> 00:11:40.166
But at least when he does
send you to war,

00:11:40.166 --> 00:11:42.534
he'll do so with this
soaring battle cry.

00:11:42.534 --> 00:11:43.902
-That is what it is.

00:11:43.902 --> 00:11:45.604
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:45.604 --> 00:11:49.140
♪♪

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:51.310 line:0%
Since this crisis started,
we've been asking people

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:53.746 line:0%
